        {
            "number": 3,
            "revision": "9e47eefa4e6516cdabf332fe5f367cd49b8e1a41",
            "parents": [
                "8810e015dc271e4c7cadafefa983ad004ae66c5f"
            ],
            "ref": "refs/changes/50/90750/3",
            "uploader": {
                "name": "Alexander",
                "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                "username": "pointbazaar"
            },
            "createdOn": 1783431148,
            "author": {
                "name": "Alexander",
                "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                "username": "pointbazaar"
            },
            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/ObjectMapper.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 275,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Is there a way to say \"all\"?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/ObjectMapper.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 275,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "Do you have a use-case?\n\nIs there a code that can handle any interface?\n\nCurrently i don't think it's implemented that way but we could easily treat the empty list as 'all interfaces'.\n\nrequesting feedback from mapper maintainers on this one."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/ObjectMapper.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 275,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "did not implement this yet as i did not find a use-case."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/ObjectMapper.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 275,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "closing this for now as no concrete use-case has been found. I don't think any caller will pass empty list of interfaces, so it remains possible to implement the suggested behavior in the future if we end up needing it."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/ObjectMapper.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 285,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Do you need the service names?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/ObjectMapper.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 285,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "For my use-case of multi-chassis fan inventory the service name was not needed.\n\nDo we have a use-case involving indexed services where it would help to know the service name as well? \n\nIt's not much more work to pass the service name as well. returning a tuple of 5 elements instead of 3.\n\nrequesting feedback from mapper maintainers on if it is acceptable to over-query or return unused data to make the call more flexible for future use-cases."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/ObjectMapper.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 285,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "How do you interact with the instance you get from the query if you don't have the service name?  You get a path but ... then what?  You have to make another mapper query to get the service that hosts that path."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/ObjectMapper.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 285,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "> How do you interact with the instance you get from the query if you don't have the service name?  \n\nIn my use-case there were other mapper calls involved while this one only figured out the overall layout.\n\nAdjusted it to also return service names to make it more widely usable."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/ObjectMapper.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 287,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "In what cases should we return ResourceNotFound vs just an empty list?  I don't really like this existing ambiguity in the mapper results.  Can we avoid errors?  Are the errors useful?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/ObjectMapper.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 287,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "The existing mapper calls look like they return that error if a nonexistent object path is passed in.\n\nIt could be implemented similarly for this new mapper call since we pass 2 object path parameters.\n\n> Can we avoid errors?  Are the errors useful?\n\ni would like to leave this to mapper maintainers, but in my use-case i do not see a benefit from extra error handling over just having an empty list."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/ObjectMapper.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 287,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "Since this is a completely new function, I'm OK with getting rid of the error and just having it return empty results."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/ObjectMapper.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 287,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                }
            ],
